cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or the results archived with it, please cite this record.
title: >-
  Analysis code and study-level data for: Perioperative Biologic Therapy in
  Psoriasis and Psoriatic Arthritis: A Systematic Review and Meta-analysis of
  Evidence Relevant to Orthopaedic Surgery
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and study-level data for a systematic review and meta-analysis
  of perioperative biologic therapy in patients with psoriasis or psoriatic
  arthritis who undergo surgery that includes orthopaedic procedures, comparing
  continued with held biologic therapy around surgery for postoperative
  infection and wound-healing complications and for skin or joint flare. The
  repository contains the R script that fits the random-effects and sensitivity
  meta-analyses and writes the summary-of-findings table and the forest plots,
  the Python scripts that draw the PRISMA flow diagram and the risk-of-bias
  figures, and a single-command driver that regenerates the results file, the
  summary-of-findings table, the sensitivity-analysis output and the figures and
  compares the regenerated numerical results with the deposited reference file.
  It also contains the extracted study-level data, the risk-of-bias assessments
  and the generated results. The data were extracted from published reports;
  no patient-level records obtained from investigators
  or health records are deposited. Every file in this repository whose name ends
  in .py, .R or .sh is licensed under the MIT License; every other file in this
  repository is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
  International licence (CC BY 4.0).
type: software
